instruction:
You are working in the repository checked out at /dayjs (a JavaScript date library, dayjs). Your goal: fix a bug in /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js.

Context from the user: There is a bug in src/plugin/weekYear/index.js. Once it is fixed, a test named `yearStart: 4` should pass; that test is NOT in the repository, its name only describes the expected behaviour.

Analysis already done (trust it):
- /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js currently is:
```js
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    return year
  }
```
- It handles the end-of-year case (December date in week 1 belongs to next year) but NOT the start-of-year case: when a locale sets `yearStart: 4` (see /dayjs/src/locale/en-gb.js, fr.js, cs.js, sk.js, zh-cn.js, zh.js and docs/en/I18n.md: "yearStart: 4 // OPTIONAL, the week that contains Jan 4th is the first week of the year"), a date in early January can belong to the LAST week (52 or 53) of the previous year, so `weekYear()` must return `year - 1`.
- Reference implementation used by this repo's tests is the `moment` package in /dayjs/node_modules (see /dayjs/test/plugin/weekYear.test.js which asserts `dayjs(day).weekYear() === moment(day).weekYear()`). E.g. `moment('2016-01-01').locale('en-gb').weekYear()` is 2015 (2016-01-01 is a Friday, ISO week 53 of 2015).

Task:
1. Add the missing case in /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js, e.g.:
```js
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
```
placed after the existing `weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11` branch. Change nothing else.
2. Verify against moment for a range of dates and locales, especially with `yearStart: 4` locales (en-gb, fr, cs, sk, zh-cn, zh) and default en. Use a TEMPORARY throwaway test file /dayjs/test/plugin/zz_weekyear_tmp.test.js (import dayjs from '../../src', moment from 'moment', extend weekYear and weekOfYear plugins from '../../src/plugin/...; import '../../src/locale/en-gb' etc.). Check dates like 2016-01-01, 2016-01-03, 2016-01-04, 2015-12-28, 2019-12-29, 2019-12-30, 2019-12-31, 2020-01-01, 2020-12-31, 2021-01-01, 2018-12-30, 2018-12-31, 2019-01-01, 2014-12-29, 2015-01-01 for locales 'en' and 'en-gb' (use `dayjs.locale(...)` / `moment.locale(...)` or the instance `.locale(...)`), comparing `weekYear()` and `week()`. Report any mismatch. Then DELETE the temp file.
3. Run the full suite: `cd /dayjs && npx jest --coverage=false 2>&1 | tail -30`. Baseline before any change: 56 suites / 524 tests all passing (a colleague has already modified src/plugin/timezone/index.js; that is expected and fine). NO pre-existing passing test may fail. Also run `npx eslint src/plugin/weekYear/index.js`.
4. Do NOT modify any pre-existing test file. Do NOT touch any other source file.

Report back: the exact diff, the commands, and their raw results (full test summary and any moment mismatches found). Be concise.

